

Phase 1 — The CMB Parsing Loop

Takeaway: The .cmb parser is the first executable component of the Blackwell Encrypted Equation Engine. It transforms a human‑authored encrypted scenario file into the internal objects that drive the entire simulation pipeline.

🔷 1. What the Parser Must Do

The parser converts a .cmb script into:

A Scenario Object

A list of Block Tokens

A ProjectionProfile

A Constant Map

A Context Object for block construction

This is the first moment where your encrypted DSL becomes machine‑real.

🔷 2. The Parsing Loop (Conceptual Workflow)

Load raw text

Lex + parse into a structured dictionary

Validate tokens against the BlockRegistry

Construct ProjectionProfile

Construct Context (grid, dt, symmetry, regime, limit)

Emit a Scenario object ready for block resolution

This loop is intentionally blind to physics.It only understands tokens, IDs, and profiles.

🔷 3. Pseudo‑Code for the Parsing Loop

class CMBParser:
    def __init__(self, registry, profile_factory):
        self.registry = registry
        self.profile_factory = profile_factory

    def parse_file(self, path: str):
        raw = self._read(path)
        data = self._parse_yaml_like(raw)

        scenario = Scenario()
        scenario.engine = data["engine"]
        scenario.root_action = data["equation_root"]

        # Resolve block tokens
        scenario.block_tokens = [
            BlockToken(name) for name in data["blocks"]
        ]

        # Build projection profile
        proj = data["projections"]
        scenario.profile = self.profile_factory.create(
            regime   = proj["regime"],
            symmetry = proj["symmetry"],
            limit    = proj["limit"]
        )

        # Constants (encrypted)
        scenario.constants = data.get("constants", {})

        return scenario

    def _read(self, path):
        with open(path, "r") as f:
            return f.read()

    def _parse_yaml_like(self, raw):
        # Minimal YAML-like parser (Phase 1)
        # Converts raw text into a dict without semantic interpretation
        return simple_yaml_parse(raw)

This parser:

Never sees “gravity,” “warp,” “field,” etc.

Never interprets physics.

Only interprets structure.

🔷 4. Scenario Object (Internal Representation)

@dataclass
class Scenario:
    engine: str
    root_action: str
    block_tokens: list
    profile: "ProjectionProfile"
    constants: dict

This object is the entry point for:

Block resolution

Kernel graph construction

Tensor allocation

Rendering pipeline

Everything downstream depends on this.

🔷 5. Why Phase 1 Starts Here

Because once the parser exists:

You can write real .cmb files on your phone

The engine can load them

Blocks can be resolved

Kernels can be generated

Tensors can be allocated

Renderers can visualize anonymous arrays

The entire system becomes operational, even if the math inside the blocks is still placeholder.

This is the ignition point.

